Wired music without crackle and with media controls (2026-10-12).

The wired iPhone sends music as 48 kHz LPCM on stream 100; Web Audio stitched 7 ms buffers (crackles
every few seconds in the car) and the head unit saw no media session. The LPCM is now framed
losslessly as FLAC (VERBATIM subframes) in fragmented MP4 and played by the same media element as
stream 102 AAC; browsers without FLAC in MSE keep the Web Audio path. check-flac.mjs proves the
framing bit-exact with ffmpeg.

